{"title":"2015 AIME I Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Diagram\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Diagram</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Computational_Geometry)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Computational Geometry)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> lies on line segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/f/3bf107349916c3ad262fe9c12a93608d845df302.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=16$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/3/a5322c7f896502c208bbb4a354efc8d212620667.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />. Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lie on the same side of line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> forming equilateral triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f75d6d58b03031bd7cb52a7ca886a8ddf369d21c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/3/423d2cdb9f74980709bf26fc4bb3cb0304964a8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BCE$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/8/5e8bc36793a7c64d05fff20d519f0f72d9256fab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AE}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/0/ce0bfc603f9a044e308b1a1fdadca917e81ad2dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" />. The area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/7/3a742217f2349beba5e71bba511cbb942726e6e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BMN$\" width=\"67\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Diagram\">Diagram</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Diagram\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/2/222ea4031f51c1923ced2de0bdf1e1f8e161a1cc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair A = (0, 0), B = (16, 0), C = (20, 0), D = (8, 8*sqrt(3)), EE = (18, 2*sqrt(3)), M = (9, sqrt(3)), NN = (14, 4*sqrt(3)); draw(A--B--D--cycle); draw(B--C--EE--cycle); draw(A--EE); draw(C--D); draw(B--M--NN--cycle); dot(A); dot(B); dot(C); dot(D); dot(EE); dot(M); dot(NN); label(&quot;A&quot;, A, SW); label(&quot;B&quot;, B, S); label(&quot;C&quot;, C, SE); label(&quot;D&quot;, D, N); label(&quot;E&quot;, EE, N); label(&quot;M&quot;, M, NW); label(&quot;N&quot;, NN, NE); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"188\" />\n</p><p>Diagram by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:RedFireTruck&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"User:RedFireTruck (page does not exist)\"><font color=\"#FF0000\">RedFireTruck</font></a> (<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User_talk:RedFireTruck\" title=\"User talk:RedFireTruck\"><font color=\"#FFFFFF\">talk</font></a>)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be the origin, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/c/93c39a18aed96da498e73643f1191da9b743ba48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B=(16,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"90\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/4/3742cfd0daafdb05cfa4b711893e9293b965833f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C=(20,0).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"95\" height=\"20\" /> Using equilateral triangle properties tells us that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/8/9284a5c46bcd6fdd9b8bdac908b6d602060acc8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D=(8,8\\sqrt3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"106\" height=\"24\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/7/1179af5f2cc96c23ab44e9f7ead5534dca3f92f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E=(18,2\\sqrt3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"114\" height=\"24\" /> as well. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/4/2d4ea1e921e86813f18c5172124b8a7d626ff7af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M=(9,\\sqrt3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/a/20ad7ea9e746f01a7473fb3c6c34dfbb509345d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N=(14,4\\sqrt3).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"121\" height=\"24\" /> Applying the Shoelace Theorem to triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/0/400eaf75c781c196c095bf559cc33680aa75c9c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BMN$\" width=\"51\" height=\"12\" /> gives\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/b/4eb795faa9474e09daaf98679a2d29d74cf3de3b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x=\\dfrac 1 2 |16\\sqrt3+36\\sqrt3+0-(0+14\\sqrt3+64\\sqrt3)| =13\\sqrt3,\\]\" width=\"441\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/c/1acea4072b601451bbef401e1e404cc9348ad587.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2=\\boxed{507}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"88\" height=\"25\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/5/2a55d61db855db32bf6056192625fd3e862f158e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=DB=16$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"124\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/1/5f12d334ae1a2dc537f27cccdebb1f0d032f4c90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE=BC=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"115\" height=\"13\" />. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/a/75a0bd9b7429b6df4a7a76d07e5ff2759aa842f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABE = \\angle DBC = 120^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"194\" height=\"13\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/9/b39af438224ff1e2e24cbd088d5d4472b8e3df38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABE \\cong \\triangle DBC$\" width=\"143\" height=\"13\" /> by SAS.\n</p><p>From this, it is clear that a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/d/08d5c45388de5c75af641c046d466de3592ffa98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" /> rotation about <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> will map <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/5/9057d4d264f5530ac63d366089bc3c17ce5d79a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABE$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/e/fee181f0e279c48906d10847f1986f902dc84efe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DBC$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />.\nThis rotation also maps <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/9/b395204f4ad6b2286cc03fb7c98eb38eba561f65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BM=BN$\" width=\"90\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/3/ea33fd1dda71abde87d266a55c3761f2652014ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle MBN=60^{\\circ}$\" width=\"112\" height=\"13\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/7/3a742217f2349beba5e71bba511cbb942726e6e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BMN$\" width=\"67\" height=\"13\" /> is equilateral.\n</p><p>Using the Law of Cosines on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/5/9057d4d264f5530ac63d366089bc3c17ce5d79a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABE$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/9/3e9cfcf470f3123f5abe24fc597ea4cc6156498d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AE^2 = 16^2 + 4^2 - 2\\cdot 16\\cdot 4\\cdot\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\]\" width=\"271\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/1/d31a376961badff7e7f841d346016e7031ac8614.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AE = 4\\sqrt{21}\\]\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" />\nThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/e/35eebd3e74505d89050e6c24fcec302cd03ee562.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM=ME=2\\sqrt{21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"158\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Using Stewart's Theorem on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/5/9057d4d264f5530ac63d366089bc3c17ce5d79a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABE$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/5/1f511908f4962923c2d3a7e2483f4b313ff9b73b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AM\\cdot ME\\cdot AE + AE\\cdot BM^2 = BE^2\\cdot AM + BA^2\\cdot ME\\]\" width=\"438\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/9/bf920dfa3a89e0ca1d6b6182d68a032fe5acacb3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[BM = 2\\sqrt{13}\\]\" width=\"101\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Calculating the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/7/3a742217f2349beba5e71bba511cbb942726e6e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BMN$\" width=\"67\" height=\"13\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/4/6f419c2618248c05d7c86be9ef01e9b3a4ffc63a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[BMN] = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} BM^2\\]\" width=\"151\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/7/4e781db0b84912cc3ca5aea6b1754d4ed879f2a5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[BMN] = 13\\sqrt{3}\\]\" width=\"126\" height=\"22\" />\nThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/e/85e42ac8c863cf6d223ca58190a5c362c5f932c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=13\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/d/71dd35fc883ec59a47e65e10e4291a385524e9f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 = 507$\" width=\"69\" height=\"15\" />. Our final answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/7/2673f497e00ae6e17e8e8f7acd64af549dcd9b9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{507}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>Admittedly, this is much more tedious than the coordinate solutions.\n</p><p>I also noticed that there are two more ways of showing that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/7/3a742217f2349beba5e71bba511cbb942726e6e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BMN$\" width=\"67\" height=\"13\" /> is equilateral:\n</p><p>One way is to show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/8/e08af8f3acc34996e3cba566dc970b7ed496ba4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADB$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/7/3a742217f2349beba5e71bba511cbb942726e6e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BMN$\" width=\"67\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/7/587303f5573fed1a511c759c6b096556daed47c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ECB$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> are related by a spiral similarity centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>The other way is to use the Mean Geometry Theorem. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/3/423d2cdb9f74980709bf26fc4bb3cb0304964a8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BCE$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/e/dae57734732e77d0de15f999bd1f4f9ee814d8a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BDA$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> are similar and have the same orientation. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is the weighted average of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the weighted average of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is the weighted average of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. The weights are the same for all three averages. (The weights are actually just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, so these are also unweighted averages.) Thus, by the Mean Geometry Theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/7/3a742217f2349beba5e71bba511cbb942726e6e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BMN$\" width=\"67\" height=\"13\" /> is similar to both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/6/1661ac6f3544a6f06f111d5e09c7072da8bb76e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BAD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/d/97dd577dd14751b09771a1c83d880f5142b86181.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BEC$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />, which means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/7/3a742217f2349beba5e71bba511cbb942726e6e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BMN$\" width=\"67\" height=\"13\" /> is equilateral.\n</p><p><br />\nNote: A much easier way to go about finding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/6/8068607716f3c2549af1dc978d77a422ca7201dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BM$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> without having to use Stewart's Theorem is to simply drop the altitudes from M and E to AC, thus hitting AC at points X and Y. Then clearly AEY and AMX are similar with ratio 2. But we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/f/dbfb501e4d1fa0c969e371211fbf54ec7e604231.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AY = 18 \\implies AX = 9 \\implies BX = 16-9 = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"373\" height=\"16\" />. Additionally, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/2/842aab96f9878557efb8fe22113c6b0b402fc882.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MX = \\frac{1}{2} (2\\sqrt{3}) = \\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"171\" height=\"38\" /> from similar triangles meaning we can now just do pythagorean theorem on right triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/7/6b70345eb69847b27d4964bf29d012e9a1f03ea0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MXB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"14\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/1/711d6cb26720a95974c11d2b6d8fcd63df6f01c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MB = \\sqrt{52}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"92\" height=\"18\" /> - SuperJJ\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2015_AIME_I_4.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/4/4a/2015_AIME_I_4.png/430px-2015_AIME_I_4.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"430\" height=\"306\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/4/4a/2015_AIME_I_4.png/645px-2015_AIME_I_4.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/4/4a/2015_AIME_I_4.png/860px-2015_AIME_I_4.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/f/b6f80d063b838c3370100d36c1632d1d847d165f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = BD, BE = BC, \\angle ABE = \\angle CBD \\implies  \\triangle ABE \\cong \\triangle DBC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"513\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Medians are equal, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/8/288326804e0b84b7edb2f8c29fcc6c2ebc646ea6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MB = BN, \\angle ABM = \\angle DBN \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"288\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/8/ba85d61c48ec910f782e25b74f14cc01d920d4e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle MBN = \\angle ABD - \\angle ABM + \\angle DBN = 60^\\circ \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"406\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/1/221a2cd89904fddc1f89bef10e60dbe283aa5666.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle MNB$\" width=\"66\" height=\"13\" /> is  equilateral triangle.\n</p><p>The height of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/3/423d2cdb9f74980709bf26fc4bb3cb0304964a8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BCE$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/3/253e0fd645030f953e6b311f887c700b485f17fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\sqrt{3},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> distance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to midpoint <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/3/9c35b1b46ddd370d3b1e5105348502503e35919a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16 + 2 = 18 \\implies \\frac {AE^2}{4} =\\frac{ (16 + 2)^2 +2^2 \\cdot 3}{4} = 81 + 3 = 84.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"464\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/6/8068607716f3c2549af1dc978d77a422ca7201dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BM$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> is the median of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/9/0e99478fa2544884c217995f7c866d9787f51aa5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABE \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/0/0e00ae0130a71d68592aec473f0d2b2136c46667.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BM^2 = \\frac {AB^2}{2} + \\frac {BE^2}{2} - \\frac {AE^2}{4}=16 \\cdot 8 + 4 \\cdot 2 - 84 = 52.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"438\" height=\"41\" /> \n</p><p>The area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/7/3a742217f2349beba5e71bba511cbb942726e6e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BMN$\" width=\"67\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/3/cb39949c73690a51fb1d97234355856723ef7f46.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[BMN] = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} BM^2 =13 \\sqrt{3} \\implies \\boxed{\\textbf{507}}.\\]\" width=\"313\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Computational_Geometry.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Computational_Geometry)\">Solution 4 (Computational Geometry)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Computational Geometry)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Take some time understanding that this solution is not a tautology of Solution 1.\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2015-MainAIME-Q4.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/8/80/2015-MainAIME-Q4.png/450px-2015-MainAIME-Q4.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"450\" height=\"305\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/8/80/2015-MainAIME-Q4.png/675px-2015-MainAIME-Q4.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/8/80/2015-MainAIME-Q4.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be the centre of the origin in the Cartesian plane. On first glance we are not given any direct correspondence of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/0/400eaf75c781c196c095bf559cc33680aa75c9c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BMN$\" width=\"51\" height=\"12\" /> to the rest of the figure, and thus for time efficiency we use computational geometry to solve this problem.\n</p><p>The line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/c/12ccedfefd0d068c168af848fa1df37806afb239.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y-\\text{intercept}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"16\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f9603ca3089464e548fc6f1366bc474e7efef8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> and thus its formula is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/1/0d1fe0afdea68630af2bda225ce5f2978b5ba0be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=mx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"11\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9adf50bf106b189e631d0b67d356b109d1d8c762.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = \\tan(-\\frac{\\pi}{3}) = -\\tan(\\frac{\\pi}{3}) = -\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"271\" height=\"34\" />. Thus, point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is located at an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> coordinate being the midpoint <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> has coordinates <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/e/8fef1aaf2d217d94ed6f2ade718c83019e47fbf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D(8, -8\\sqrt{3})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"96\" height=\"24\" />. Line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/c/13c970cbf5e2e7029089517d5e8efbb8cade6d8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> has a positive incline passing through the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/6/426e617b28087d18baf8111d910121814cdd945b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C(20,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"66\" height=\"20\" />. It follows that the slope of said line is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/3/e03c0c2e8c044fbaa2b0e88b0b43e9fc01f2271d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(\\frac{\\pi}{6}) = \\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"106\" height=\"34\" />. From there, the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/c/12ccedfefd0d068c168af848fa1df37806afb239.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y-\\text{intercept}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"16\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is determined by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/2/9221824d338b38a92384990687db80d6d344c8c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-20\\sqrt{3} = b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"90\" height=\"21\" />, and thus point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> whose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> coordinate is 18 satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/c/4ac3e69bf6c60bab93650791f455fbcce221933b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E(18,-2\\sqrt{3})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"104\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p><p>Through midpoint formulae on both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a65c05bd85d2609bea5db2b109ed5f556463511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/0/240c8b05d00d6baa14c841afc1b7728c86e653cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M(14, -4\\sqrt{3})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"109\" height=\"24\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/3/393b30ab0f3dc663f62307d840874081beb5e613.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N(9, -\\sqrt{3})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"88\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p><p>Finally, Shoelace formula on figure <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/0/400eaf75c781c196c095bf559cc33680aa75c9c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BMN$\" width=\"51\" height=\"12\" /> yields the desired <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/a/aca8512ad483523809f47c628b2c02cd71c703ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{X} = 13\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"21\" />, thus implying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/1/901f1a6e70daf9c46a959cde95b1f19d12c16348.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{X}^2 = \\boxed{507}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"88\" height=\"25\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cf65b1f2fbdf388e3daeff9b96b34d3399d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I\" title=\"2015 AIME I\">2015 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2015 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2015 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2015\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2015 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2015 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n